use std
into spring.amni

Imports: gfx, math, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.motion and gfx.scene3d. This file is a module with no main. It is a port of the spring-bone solver in web/js/avatar.js (`springs`, `side`, `aim`): hair braids, face-framing locks, hoodie cords and skirt panels swing on chains of glTF bones named like `braid_0`, `braid_1`, … or `lock3_0`, `lock3_1`, …. All positions are in world space unless they say rest; rest positions are in the skin's bind space. Normalize every vector with `linalg::unit3`; rotate vectors with `linalg::qrotate`; multiply quaternions with `linalg::qmul`; points through matrices with `linalg::point`, directions with `linalg::direction`.

Struct `Par` holds st, gr, inr, bend, rad (each f32), ns (int), ring, follow and cap0 (each f32).

`par(g int) Par` returns the settings of spring group g: group 1 (lock) is st 0.9, gr 0.8, inr 0.6, bend 0.6, rad 0.006, ns 250, ring 0, follow 0, cap0 0; group 2 (cord) is st 0.4, gr 1.2, inr 0.7, bend 0.9, rad 0.004, ns 250, ring 0, follow 0, cap0 0; group 3 (skirt) is st 2.4, gr 0.35, inr 0.5, bend 0.45, rad 0.02, ns 1, ring 1.04, follow 0.85, cap0 0.25; anything else (group 0, braid) is st 0.7, gr 1.0, inr 0.6, bend 0.7, rad 0.011, ns 170, ring 0, follow 0, cap0 0.

`group_of(name const byte[:]) int` maps a group name to its number: "braid" 0, "lock" 1, "cord" 2, "skirt" 3, anything else 0.

`starts(s const byte[:], p const byte[:]) bool` is true when s begins with p.

`surf_ok(g int, mesh const byte[:]) bool` says whether a mesh's vertices are collision surface for group g: group 0 when the name starts with any of "skin", "tank", "tank_hem", "outfit", "hoodie", "shirt" or "jacket"; group 1 when the name equals "skin" or "face"; group 2 when it starts with "hoodie", "outfit" or "skin"; group 3 never.

`pick(g int, x f32, nz f32) bool` chooses surface vertices by rest x and rest normal z: group 0 when `abs(x) < 0.11 && nz < -0.3`; group 1 when `abs(x) > 0.04 && nz > -0.2`; group 2 when `abs(x) < 0.09 && nz > 0.3`; group 3 never.

`clamp01(v f32) f32` clamps v to [0, 1].

`qconj(q linalg::Quat) linalg::Quat` is the conjugate (x, y, z negated, w kept).

`qfrom(a float3, b float3) linalg::Quat` is the shortest rotation taking unit vector a to unit vector b: with `r = dot3(a, b) + 1`, when r < 0.000001 use axis `unit3(cross3(v3(1, 0, 0), a))` (or `unit3(cross3(v3(0, 1, 0), a))` when that cross product is shorter than 0.000001) and return `Quat { axis.x, axis.y, axis.z, 0 }`; otherwise `c = cross3(a, b)` and return `linalg::qnorm(Quat { c.x, c.y, c.z, r })`.

`mquat(m gfx::mat4) linalg::Quat` is the rotation part of a matrix with uniform scale: take the first three components of columns c0, c1, c2, normalize each, and convert the 3x3 rotation (column j is the image of axis j, so element (row i, column j) is column j's component i) to a quaternion with the standard trace method (trace > 0 branch, then the largest diagonal element branch), then `linalg::qnorm`.

`pos(m gfx::mat4) float3` is the translation, `m.c3.xyz`.

Module state: `var chains = 0`, `var item = -1`, `var sk = -1` (the skin), `var place_rot = linalg::quat_identity()`; per chain (index c below `chains`): `var ch_g int[>..]`, `var ch_first int[>..]` (first slot in the per-bone arrays), `var ch_n int[>..]` (bones in the chain), `var ch_order int[>..]` (the number after the group name in the first bone's name, 0 when none), `var ch_ready bool[>..]`, `var ch_fo f32[>..]` (follow weight, 0 when none), `var ch_wl f32[>..]`; per bone slot: `var b_node int[>..]` (global glTF node), `var b_rq linalg::Quat[>..]` (rest local rotation), `var b_off float3[>..]` (rest local translation), `var b_len f32[>..]` (length of b_off), `var b_cur float3[>..]`, `var b_prev float3[>..]`, `var b_c0 float3[>..]`, `var b_ul float3[>..]`, `var b_ur float3[>..]`, `var b_colb int[>..]` (body node the point collides against, -1 none), `var b_coln float3[>..]`; capsules: `var cap_g int[>..]`, `var cap_a int[>..]`, `var cap_b int[>..]`, `var cap_r0 f32[>..]`, `var cap_r1 f32[>..]`, `var cap_pa float3[>..]`, `var cap_pb float3[>..]`; surface samples: `var s_g int[>..]`, `var s_v int[>..]` (vertex index in `gltf::verts`, `VERTEX_FLOATS` floats each), `var s_w float3[>..]`; `var pal gfx::mat4[>..]`; ring rest distances `var rd f32[>..]` per bone slot (`var rd_ready = false`); thighs `var th = int[4] { -1, -1, -1, -1 }` (thigh_l, thigh_r, calf_l, calf_r); `var warm = false`.

`ibm(node int) int` returns the index into `gltf::matrices` of the node's inverse bind matrix in skin `sk` (scan `gltf::skins[sk].joints`: the joint k with `gltf::ints[joints.first + k] == node` gives `inverse_binds.first + k`), or -1 when the node is not a joint or sk < 0. `joint_of(node int) int` returns that k (or -1).

`rp(node int) float3` is the rest position `pos(linalg::inverse(gltf::matrices[ibm(node)]))`; `rrot(node int) linalg::Quat` is `mquat(linalg::inverse(gltf::matrices[ibm(node)]))`. Callers check `ibm(node) >= 0` first.

`find(asset int, name const byte[:]) int` is `gltf::find_node(asset, name)`.

`md(xs f32[>..]&) f32` returns 0.07 when xs is empty, else sorts xs ascending (plain insertion sort) and returns the element at index `floor(len * 0.99)` clamped to `len - 1`.

`spring_open(asset int, it int) int` builds everything once and returns `chains`. Set `item = it`. Choose the skin: the node of the asset named "skin" when it has a mesh and `skin >= 0`, else the first node of the asset with a mesh and a skin; set `sk` to that node's skin (return 0 when none) and remember the node as `skin_node`. Chains: for every node n of the asset (`gltf::assets[asset].nodes.first + k`), with `nm = gltf::text_of(gltf::nodes[n].name)`, a chain starts at n when nm is at least 3 bytes, ends with "_0", everything before the "_0" is lowercase letters followed by optional digits (at least one letter first), no node is named nm without its last two bytes, and a node named nm with its final "0" replaced by "2" exists. Its base is nm without the final "0" (for example "lock3_"); its bones are the nodes named base + "0", base + "1", … for as long as they exist (stop at the first missing one, at most 64). Its group name is base with the trailing "_" and then any trailing digits removed ("lock3_" → "lock"); `ch_order` is the integer value of those removed digits (0 when there are none). Push one slot per bone: b_node the node, b_rq `gltf::nodes[node].r`, b_off `gltf::nodes[node].t`, b_len `length3` of it, b_cur, b_prev, b_c0, b_ul, b_ur and b_coln zero vectors, b_colb -1, rd 0. Push the chain's g, first slot, n, order, ready false, fo 0, wl 0.
Body bones for collision: the nodes named "head", "neck_01", "spine_03", "spine_02", "spine_01" and "pelvis" in that order, keeping those that exist and have `ibm >= 0`. For each chain and each bone slot k from 1 to n - 1: with `p = rp(node)` (skip when ibm < 0), pick the body bone b whose `abs(rp(b).y - p.y)` is smallest (the first one wins ties), set b_colb to b and b_coln to `unit3(v3(p.x - rp(b).x, 0, p.z - rp(b).z))`.
Thighs: th = the nodes "thigh_l", "thigh_r", "calf_l", "calf_r"; when any is missing or thigh_l or thigh_r has ibm < 0, set th[0] = -1. With `pv` = rp of "pelvis" (when it exists with ibm >= 0), for each chain whose `par(g).follow > 0`, when th[0] >= 0 and pv exists and the first bone has ibm >= 0: `r0 = rp(first bone)`, `nrm = unit3(v3(r0.x - pv.x, 0, r0.z - pv.z))`, `ch_fo = clamp01((nrm.z + 0.55) * 1.3) * follow`, `ch_wl = clamp01(0.5 + r0.x / 0.06)`; with `il = qconj(rrot(th[0]))`, `ir = qconj(rrot(th[1]))`, for each bone slot k below n - 1 (when both it and the next bone have ibm >= 0): `dm = unit3(rp(next) - rp(this))`, b_ul = `qrotate(il, dm)`, b_ur = `qrotate(ir, dm)`.
Capsules: for group 3 only (when some chain has g == 3), add a capsule for each pair (thigh_l, calf_l) and (thigh_r, calf_r) when both nodes exist and the first has ibm >= 0: `A = rp(a)`, `B = rp(b)`, `ab = B - A`, `bi = joint_of(a)`; over every vertex v of every primitive of `skin_node`'s mesh (from `prim.vfirst` for `prim.vcount` vertices, floats at `v * gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS`: position 0..2, joints 18..21 as floats, weights 22..25), w = the sum of the weights whose joint equals bi; skip when w < 0.6; `x = p - A`; `t = dot3(x, ab) / dot3(ab, ab)`; skip when t < 0 or t > 1; `r = length3(x - ab * t)`; push r to a list `lo` when t < 0.35 and to `hi` when t > 0.65. r0 = `min(md(lo), md(hi) * 1.1)`, r1 = `md(hi)`. Push cap_g 3, a, b, r0, r1 and two zero vectors.
Surface samples: for each group g used by some chain: `y0` = the smallest rest y over all its chains' bones (with ibm >= 0) minus 0.05, `y1` the largest; for each node of the asset with a mesh and `skin == sk` whose mesh name passes `surf_ok(g, name)`, collect the vertices v of all its primitives whose rest y (float 1) is strictly between y0 and y1 and pass `pick(g, x, nz)` with x float 0 and nz the normal's z (float 5); with `st = max(1, (count + ns - 1) / ns)` for that mesh, keep every collected vertex whose position j in the collected list has `j % st == 0`, pushing s_g g, s_v v and a zero s_w.
Return chains.

`refresh(i int)` recomputes one node's world matrix from its parent: with `p = gltf::nodes[i].parent`, `motion::world[i] = gfx::mul(if p >= 0 { motion::world[p] } else { s3d::items[item].place }, motion::local_matrix(i))`.

`wrot(i int) linalg::Quat` is `mquat(motion::world[i])`.

`side(p float3, c float3, a float3, l float3, h float3) float3`: `n = unit3(l)`; `s = h - a`; `s = s - n * dot3(s, n)`; `k = length3(s)`; when k < 0.000001 return p; `s = s / k`; `d = dot3(p - c, s)`; return `p - s * (2 * d)` when d < 0, else p.

`fix(nx float3, hw float3, l f32) float3` is `hw + unit3(nx - hw) * l` (keeps a point at length l from hw).

`caps_push(g int, nx float3, hw float3, s f32, rad f32, l f32, its int) float3`: repeat `its` times: for each capsule z of group g: `lt = cap_pb[z] - cap_pa[z]`; `t = clamp01(dot3(nx - cap_pa[z], lt) / dot3(lt, lt))`; `r = (cap_r0[z] + (cap_r1[z] - cap_r0[z]) * t + rad) * s`; `d = cap_pa[z] + lt * t`; when `length3(nx - d) < r`: `nx = side(nx, d, cap_pa[z], lt, hw)`, `nx = d + unit3(nx - d) * r`, `nx = fix(nx, hw, l)`. Return nx.

`aim(c int)`: for each bone slot k from 0 to n - 2 of chain c (slot `f = ch_first[c] + k`, node `b = b_node[f]`): `motion::pose_r[b] = b_rq[f]`; `refresh(b)`; `hw = pos(motion::world[b])`; `pq = wrot(gltf::nodes[b].parent)`; `wq = qmul(pq, b_rq[f])`; `d0 = qrotate(wq, unit3(b_off[f + 1]))`; `d = unit3(b_cur[f + 1] - hw)`; `motion::pose_r[b] = qmul(qconj(pq), qmul(qfrom(d0, d), wq))`; `refresh(b)`.

`step(dt f32)` advances every chain once. `h = min(dt, 1 / 30)`. Skin the surface samples: `motion::joints(sk, pal)`; for each sample i with `o = s_v[i] * gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS`, `p = v3(verts[o], verts[o + 1], verts[o + 2])`, `s_w[i] = sum over j in 0..3 of verts[o + 22 + j] * linalg::point(pal[verts[o + 18 + j] as int], p)`. Thigh gating when th[0] >= 0: `ql = wrot(th[0])`, `qr = wrot(th[1])`, and `ga(a, b) = clamp01((acos(clamp(-unit3(pos(world[b]) - pos(world[a])).y, -1, 1)) - 0.6) / 0.45)`, `gl = ga(th[0], th[2])`, `gr = ga(th[1], th[3])` (both 0 without thighs). Set every capsule's `cap_pa = pos(world[cap_a])`, `cap_pb = pos(world[cap_b])`, then `cap_pa = mix3(cap_pa, cap_pb, par(cap_g).cap0)`. `var pd = v3(0, -1, 0)`.
For each chain c with `K = par(ch_g[c])`, `n = ch_n[c]`, `f0 = ch_first[c]`, `S = length3(world[b_node[f0]].c0.xyz)`: when `!ch_ready[c] || h <= 0`: set `motion::pose_r` of every bone of the chain to its b_rq and `refresh` them in order; for slots 1..n-1 set b_cur and b_prev to the bone's world position; when not ch_ready also set b_c0 the same; set ch_ready true. Then for k from 0 to n - 2 (slot `f = f0 + k`, node `b = b_node[f]`, next slot `f1 = f + 1`): `motion::pose_r[b] = b_rq[f]`; `refresh(b)`; `hw = pos(world[b])`; `pq = wrot(gltf::nodes[b].parent)`; `wq = qmul(pq, b_rq[f])`; `d0 = qrotate(wq, unit3(b_off[f1]))`; when `ch_fo[c] > 0 && gl + gr > 0`: `wl = ch_wl[c]`, `u = unit3(mix3(qrotate(ql, b_ul[f]), qrotate(qr, b_ur[f]), 1 - wl))`, `d0 = unit3(mix3(d0, u, ch_fo[c] * (gl * wl + gr * (1 - wl))))`. `L = b_len[f1] * S`; `p = b_cur[f1]`; `q = b_prev[f1]`; `nx = p + (p - q) * K.inr + d0 * (K.st * h * L / 0.05) + v3(0, -1, 0) * (K.gr * h * L / 0.05)`; `nx = fix(nx, hw, L)`. When k > 0: `d = unit3(nx - hw)`; `a = acos(clamp(dot3(d, pd), -1, 1))`; when `a > K.bend`: `ax = cross3(pd, d)`, and when `length3(ax) > 0.000001`, `nx = hw + qrotate(linalg::qaxis(unit3(ax), K.bend), pd) * L`. Then `nx = caps_push(ch_g[c], nx, hw, S, K.rad, L, 3)`. Surface: when `b_colb[f1] >= 0`: `nb = unit3(linalg::direction(world[b_colb[f1]], b_coln[f1]))`; repeat 3 times: `top = -1000000000`; for each sample i with `s_g[i] == ch_g[c]`: `lt = s_w[i] - nx`, `a = dot3(lt, nb)`, when `dot3(lt - nb * a, lt - nb * a) < 0.0013` set `top = max(top, dot3(s_w[i], nb))`; `e = top + K.rad * S - dot3(nx, nb)`; when e > 0, `nx = fix(nx + nb * e, hw, L)`. Then `d = unit3(nx - hw)`; `pd = d`; `b_prev[f1] = p`; `b_cur[f1] = nx`; `motion::pose_r[b] = qmul(qconj(pq), qmul(qfrom(d0, d), wq))`; `refresh(b)`.
Rings: for each group g with `par(g).ring > 0` that has at least 3 chains: list its chains sorted by ch_order ascending (the ring order; the last links back to the first). When `!rd_ready`, for each listed chain a with next chain o and each slot index k from 1 to `min(n_a, n_o) - 1`, set `rd[first_a + k] = length3(b_c0[first_a + k] - b_c0[first_o + k])`; set rd_ready true after all ring groups. With `S` from the group's first chain as above, repeat 4 times: (1) for each listed chain a with next o, for k from 1 to `min(n_a, n_o) - 1`: `pa = b_cur[first_a + k]`, `qo = b_cur[first_o + k]`, `L = rd[first_a + k] * par(g).ring * S`, `d = qo - pa`, `e = length3(d)`; when e > L: `d = d * ((e - L) / e / 2)`, `b_cur[first_a + k] = pa + d`, `b_cur[first_o + k] = qo - d`. (2) for each listed chain a: `hw = pos(world[b_node[first_a]])`; for k from 1 to n_a - 1: `L = b_len[first_a + k] * S`, `h0 = if k > 1 { b_cur[first_a + k - 1] } else { hw }`, `p = fix(b_cur[first_a + k], h0, L)`; for each capsule z of group g: `lt = cap_pb[z] - cap_pa[z]`, `t = clamp01(dot3(p - cap_pa[z], lt) / dot3(lt, lt))`, `r = (cap_r0[z] + (cap_r1[z] - cap_r0[z]) * t + par(g).rad) * S`, `d = cap_pa[z] + lt * t`, and when `length3(p - d) < r`: `p = side(p, d, cap_pa[z], lt, hw)`, `p = fix(d + unit3(p - d) * r, h0, L)`; store `b_cur[first_a + k] = p`. After the 4 rounds call `aim` for each listed chain.

`spring_step(dt f32)` first returns without doing anything when chains is 0 or when `length3(motion::world[b_node[ch_first[0]]].c0.xyz)` is below 0.001 (the page has not sent a pose yet, so the bones are degenerate); otherwise it runs `step(dt)`; the first time it is called (`!warm`) it sets `warm = true` and then runs `step(1 / 60)` 20 more times. Afterwards, for every chain and every bone slot k below n - 1, call `s3d::set_node(item, b_node[slot], motion::pose_t[b_node[slot]], motion::pose_r[b_node[slot]], motion::pose_s[b_node[slot]])`.
